  "manual_review": {
    "positive_findings": [
      "Three genuinely different deterministic crown forms replace the single repeated scaffold.",
      "All three variants are represented across the existing source HISM components without changing source transforms or production ecology authority.",
      "Each mesh has validated descending near, mid, and far render LODs with masked dither transitions.",
      "Bounded AO and normal response reduce uniform black crushing without emissive or unlit compensation."
    ],
    "rejection_reasons": [
      "Sparse planar leaf clusters remain visibly separate from exposed procedural limbs rather than reading as continuous interior-live-oak foliage volume.",
      "Troublemaker and Coloma still expose geometric fork patterns and broad card silhouettes despite the morphology variation.",
      "Far Salmon Falls silhouettes fragment into isolated dark bars and clumps; fixed frames do not establish a temporally stable moving-camera transition.",
      "Component-level selection cannot break repetition inside each large HISM batch.",
      "Terrain, water, other foliage, lighting, and material integration remain synthetic, so no frame is acceptable release media."
    ],
    "decision": "Reject v212 visual promotion. Retain the deterministic crown-family generator, stable review distribution, calibrated lit-material option, alpha-coverage import fix, explicit LOD authoring, and pinned captures as technical infrastructure only.",
    "next_required_visual_input": "Stop tuning this procedural scaffold. Intake rights-reviewed production tree geometry or an art-authored botanical trunk, branch, twig, and volumetric shoot set with multiple age forms; support per-instance variation, root and understory integration, temporal transition review, and named art plus ecology approval."
  },
